# oxfmt's ignore file (`oxfmt --check` reads .gitignore and .prettierignore).
#
# docs/research/ holds verbatim research digests and audit transcripts kept as
# evidence for the ETHOnline submission. Reformatting them rewrites the record:
# oxfmt canonicalises GFM ambiguities in the source text (single `~` into `~~`
# strikethrough, `*` emphasis into `_`), which changes the bytes a judge reads.
docs/research/

# Idea rounds written by another tool and kept unedited for provenance.
docs/plan/archive/IDEAS.md
docs/plan/archive/IDEAS_KIMI.md
docs/plan/archive/IDEAS_V3_KIMI.md

# Skill mirrors that a workspace tool drops into every repository it opens.
# Not part of this build and not tracked; kept out of the formatter so the gate
# does not depend on files nobody here wrote.
.claude/
.codex/
.grok/

# Vendored skills installed through skills-lock.json (the hyperframes video
# pack and its media tooling, 900-odd files nobody here wrote). Kept tracked so
# the lock resolves, kept out of the formatter and linter so the gate judges
# our code and not theirs. The repository's own skills stay formatted.
.agents/skills/
!.agents/skills/froggy-browser/
!.agents/skills/froggy-leash/
